From 262343aeb2011823c01b9bf928ba8570c1a7ad9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cs2_scout owner <tpoofh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:52:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Coverage repair: every listed match, resumable listings,
 staged dataset revisions

- Crawl scope: drop "both teams in today's top N" (pipeline.relevant). Every non-forfeit listed
  result is queued; --top is optional and means EITHER team tracked, matched by HLTV team id
  (exact names resolved to ids, never fuzzy). Defaults 0 for update/watch/results/backfill;
  watch.yml, docker-compose and the failsafe listings follow.
- Listings never stop silently: a failed page (or a catch-up cap) raises ListingIncomplete with
  what was found, saves listing_cursor:<source>:<start>:<end> in scraper_state, and the next run
  resumes there. Catch-up stops only on a page with nothing unseen. Health check
  listing_incomplete (error after 6 h).
- result_manifest (append-only): discovered / present / skipped / stored / waiting /
  unavailable / failed per listed match; result_manifest_state view for accounting. Matches still
  without statistics 7 days after they were played (two looks) become 'unavailable', final.
- raw_pages / mapstats_pages: first_fetched_at written once (trigger rejects changes),
  fetched_at = latest, refetched_at; older rows stay NULL instead of an invented time.
- created_revision_id / updated_revision_id on the stat tables.
- Staged dataset revisions (hltv_scraper/revisions.py): `revision create` registers
  hltv_meta.dataset_revisions and builds schema hltv_rev_<n> as a copy of public (fingerprints of
  live matches kept); --revision N / HLTV_REVISION puts only that schema on the search path;
  `backfill` lists the window (global + board teams, opponents, players, former teams);
  `revision status|accept|seal|promote|discard`. Promotion is a separate owner-approved step that
  only adds the revision's matches to public. Dated `update` against live is refused.
- backfill.yml rewritten for staged revisions (list, scrape, expand, scrape2, mapstats, report).
- Tests: tests/test_coverage.py (offline), tests/test_revisions.py (PostgreSQL);
  scripts/acceptance_staged.sql for psql.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
