@@ -359,6 +364,21 @@ minute-by-minute lines run the receiver above.
 - `live-check.yml`: daily live scrape of rankings, results, a match page and the schedule with the
   `flaresolverr`, `camoufox` and `scrapling` backends, so layout or Cloudflare changes are caught early.
 - `tests.yml`: the test suite (offline fixtures + PostgreSQL) on every push.
+- `backfill.yml`: history backfill into a staged dataset revision (never the live tables), spread
+  over up to 8 machines; rerun with the revision id until its report passes.
+
+## Dataset revisions
+
+A backfill writes into its own schema `hltv_rev_<n>` (registered in `hltv_meta.dataset_revisions`
+with its job, git commit, arguments, counts and completeness), created as a copy of the live tables
+so the revision is "live + backfill". `--revision n` (or `HLTV_REVISION=n`) puts only that schema
+on the search path. Every stat row carries `created_revision_id` / `updated_revision_id` (NULL for
+rows copied from live), every listed result is logged in the append-only `result_manifest`
+(discovered, present, skipped, stored, waiting, unavailable, failed), and archived pages keep their
+first fetch time (`first_fetched_at`, never rewritten - a trigger rejects changes).
+`revision seal n` makes a complete revision read-only; `revision promote n --confirm hltv_rev_n
+--approved-by NAME` (owner-approved, after review) copies the matches it added into the live tables
+without changing anything already there.
 
